      <Xref identifier="Q9FVI8" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="215" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">Partial protein lacking the first 36 amino acids of the polypeptide. These 36 acids are postulated to be part of the targeting signal. Therefore the truncation does not affect the mature protein studied in &lt;i&gt;E.coli&lt;/i&gt; |CITS: [10700382]|. &amp;beta;-Myrcene is the main conversion product catalyzed by TPS10 (56%), followed by (&lt;i&gt;E&lt;/i&gt;)-&amp;beta;-ocimene (20%) and minor amounts of cyclic monoterpenes (each less than 5%): limonene, 2-carene and tricyclene |CITS: [10700382]|.</Comment>
